  "reason": "The evidence strongly establishes scvi_n200 as the dominant RNA encoder (0.71–0.73 vs 0.51–0.52 for scgpt), and the current best (config_003, acc=0.725) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted. However, all scvi_n200 experiments to date have used transformer aggregation; no avgpool variant has been tested with this encoder. Config_007 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) is a clean, single-variable change from the current best, directly testing whether the transformer aggregation is truly necessary or whether a simpler pooling strategy matches or exceeds it. If avgpool performs comparably, it confirms robustness and frees a later experiment for finer-tuning; if it underperforms, it confirms transformer is critical and narrows the search. With 3 experiments remaining after this one, reducing uncertainty on the aggregation dimension—while holding the other three parameters at their best-known values—is the highest-information use of this slot."
}

